-- cases/user-guide-appendix-ii.l4 — YC's own worked examples as tests (SPEC.md §7).
--
-- Source: "SAFE User Guide", Appendix II, Example 1 (two post-money Safes), pp. 19–23 of
-- the PDF fetched 2026-09-04. The guide rounds the option pool increase to the nearest
-- thousand shares and prices to four decimals, and computes onward from the rounded
-- figures; this encoding keeps exact rationals and rounds shares down once, at the end
-- (fork F3). So Company Capitalization and the cap-method share counts, which do not
-- depend on the rounded price, are asserted exactly; the price, pool increase, new-money
-- shares and pro rata shares are asserted to within 0.05% of the guide's printed figures.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `safe-form`
IMPORT safe
IMPORT `safe-portfolio`

§ `Tolerance`

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
      y IS A NUMBER
      tolerance IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `close to` x y tolerance IF
    x MINUS y AT MOST tolerance TIMES y AND y MINUS x AT MOST tolerance TIMES y

GIVEN c IS A Conversion
      who IS A STRING
GIVETH A NUMBER
`shares for` c who MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN r YIELD r's shares) (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's investor EQUALS who) (c's rows)))

GIVEN c IS A Conversion
      who IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`method for` c who MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's investor EQUALS who) (c's rows)
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN r's method
    WHEN EMPTY THEN "absent"

§ `Example 1 — ABC, Inc.`

-- "ABC, Inc. (the “Company”) raised $1,000,000 from two investors. Investor A purchased a
-- $200,000 safe at a $4m post-money valuation cap safe and Investor B purchased an
-- $800,000 safe at an $8m post-money valuation cap." — p. 19
-- Cap table immediately prior: Founders 9,250,000; options outstanding 300,000; promised
-- options 350,000; options available 100,000; fully diluted 10,000,000.

nobody MEANS Signatory WITH
    name  IS "—"
    title IS "—"

GIVEN who IS A STRING
GIVETH A Party
`party named` who MEANS Party WITH
    name      IS who
    address   IS ""
    email     IS ""
    signatory IS nobody

`ABC cap table` MEANS CapTableIn WITH
    commonOutstanding  IS 9_250_000
    optionsOutstanding IS 300_000
    promisedOptions    IS 350_000
    unissuedOptionPool IS 100_000

`ABC` MEANS CompanyIn WITH
    name               IS "ABC, Inc."
    incorporation      IS JUST "Delaware"
    governingLaw       IS JUST "Delaware"
    registrationNumber IS NOTHING
    address            IS ""
    email              IS ""
    signatory          IS nobody
    capTable           IS `ABC cap table`

`US cap form` MEANS FormIn WITH
    family       IS "postmoney"
    edition      IS "1.2"
    jurisdiction IS "us"
    variant      IS "cap"

`safe A` MEANS SafeIn WITH
    investor          IS `party named` "Investor A"
    purchaseAmount    IS 200_000
    date              IS "2018-10-01"
    terms             IS `cap terms` 4_000_000
    proRataSideLetter IS FALSE

`safe B` MEANS SafeIn WITH
    investor          IS `party named` "Investor B"
    purchaseAmount    IS 800_000
    date              IS "2018-10-01"
    terms             IS `cap terms` 8_000_000
    proRataSideLetter IS TRUE

GIVEN cap IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A TermsIn
`cap terms` cap MEANS TermsIn WITH
    cap      IS JUST cap
    discount IS NOTHING
    mfn      IS NOTHING

§§ `Q1 — no round yet: the implied dilution`

`before any round` MEANS Deal WITH
    form    IS `US cap form`
    company IS `ABC`
    safes   IS LIST `safe A`, `safe B`
    round   IS NOTHING

#EVAL `validate deal` `before any round`
#ASSERT null (`validate deal` `before any round`)

-- "Company Capitalization = … = 10,000,000 / (100% - 15%) = 11,764,705" — p. 20
#EVAL (convert `before any round`)'s companyCapitalization
#ASSERT `close to` ((convert `before any round`)'s companyCapitalization) 11_764_705 0.0001

-- "Investor A’s shares = 11,764,705 * 5% = 588,235 … Investor B’s shares = 11,764,705 * 10% = 1,176,470" — p. 20
#ASSERT `shares for` (convert `before any round`) "Investor A" EQUALS 588_235
#ASSERT `shares for` (convert `before any round`) "Investor B" EQUALS 1_176_470

§§ `Q2 — a $5m Series A at $15m pre-money, 10% post-closing pool`

-- "Pre-money valuation: $15,000,000; Total raise (new cash): $5,000,000; Target available
--  option pool: 10%; Option pool increase: 1,695,000 shares; Series A price per share:
--  $1.1144" — p. 19. "Investor C, the lead investor, will be investing $4m".

`series A` MEANS RoundIn WITH
    name              IS "Series A"
    preMoneyValuation IS 15_000_000
    newMoney          IS 5_000_000
    targetPoolPercent IS 10
    lead              IS JUST (LeadIn WITH name IS "Investor C", amount IS 4_000_000)

`example 1 Q2` MEANS Deal WITH
    form    IS `US cap form`
    company IS `ABC`
    safes   IS LIST `safe A`, `safe B`
    round   IS JUST `series A`

#EVAL convert `example 1 Q2`

-- Both Safes convert at their caps: the round price exceeds both Safe Prices.
#ASSERT `method for` (convert `example 1 Q2`) "Investor A" EQUALS "cap"
#ASSERT `method for` (convert `example 1 Q2`) "Investor B" EQUALS "cap"
#ASSERT `shares for` (convert `example 1 Q2`) "Investor A" EQUALS 588_235
#ASSERT `shares for` (convert `example 1 Q2`) "Investor B" EQUALS 1_176_470

-- The guide's 1,695,000 is its own rounding of 1,694,570 to the thousand (F3).
#ASSERT `close to` ((convert `example 1 Q2`)'s optionPoolIncrease) 1_695_000 0.0005
#ASSERT `close to` ((convert `example 1 Q2`)'s standardPrice) 1.1144 0.0005
-- "The Company will sell 4,486,719 shares of Series A Preferred Stock" — p. 20
#ASSERT `close to` ((convert `example 1 Q2`)'s newMoneyShares) 4_486_719 0.0005
-- "Investor B’s pro rata = 4,486,719 * 10% = 448,671 shares … for $499,998.97" — p. 20
#ASSERT `close to` (sum (map (GIVEN p YIELD p's shares) ((convert `example 1 Q2`)'s proRata))) 448_671 0.0005

§§ `Q5 — a $2.2m Series Seed at $8.8m pre-money: one Safe switches to the round price`

-- "Investor C, the lead investor, will be investing $1.65m" — p. 22. "(2) Safe Price"
-- wins for Investor A and "(1) Series Seed price per share" wins for Investor B, and A's
-- Company Capitalization is recomputed as (10,000,000 + 1,216,360) / (100% − 5%) =
-- 11,806,694, giving A 590,334 shares — p. 23. The guide's B figure carries its rounded
-- price ($0.6577) and rounded pool increase (1,573,000); the exact fixpoint gives
-- 11,806,59x and B 1,216,2xx, within 0.05%.

`series Seed` MEANS RoundIn WITH
    name              IS "Series Seed"
    preMoneyValuation IS 8_800_000
    newMoney          IS 2_200_000
    targetPoolPercent IS 10
    lead              IS JUST (LeadIn WITH name IS "Investor C", amount IS 1_650_000)

`example 1 Q5` MEANS Deal WITH
    form    IS `US cap form`
    company IS `ABC`
    safes   IS LIST `safe A`, `safe B`
    round   IS JUST `series Seed`

#EVAL convert `example 1 Q5`

#ASSERT `method for` (convert `example 1 Q5`) "Investor A" EQUALS "cap"
#ASSERT `method for` (convert `example 1 Q5`) "Investor B" EQUALS "price"
#ASSERT `close to` ((convert `example 1 Q5`)'s companyCapitalization) 11_806_694 0.0005
#ASSERT `close to` (`shares for` (convert `example 1 Q5`) "Investor A") 590_334 0.0005
#ASSERT `close to` (`shares for` (convert `example 1 Q5`) "Investor B") 1_216_360 0.0005
#ASSERT `close to` ((convert `example 1 Q5`)'s standardPrice) 0.6577 0.0005
#ASSERT `close to` ((convert `example 1 Q5`)'s optionPoolIncrease) 1_573_000 0.0005

-- How many passes the partition needed. The guide stops after one and a half.
#EVAL `passes used` `example 1 Q5` EMPTY 3

§§ `Q3 — acquired for $10m cash before any Equity Financing`

-- "Investor A’s Conversion Amount = $200,000 / ($4,000,000 / (9,550,000 / 85%)) = 561,764
--  Investor B’s Conversion Amount = … = 1,123,529
--  The per share cash consideration for all stockholders, if the safes convert, is $0.8901
--  ($10,000,000 divided by the Liquidity Capitalization of 11,235,293). … both safes would
--  automatically convert … Investor A’s share of cash consideration = 561,764 * $0.8901 =
--  $500,026; Investor B’s … = $1,000,053" — p. 21. Promised options are zeroed (n. 3).

`acquired for 10m` MEANS LiquidityIn WITH
    proceeds                         IS 10_000_000
    indebtedness                     IS 0
    promisedOptionsReceivingProceeds IS 0

GIVEN l IS A Liquidity
      who IS A STRING
GIVETH A LiquidityRow
`liquidity row for` l who MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's investor EQUALS who) (l's rows)
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN r
    WHEN EMPTY THEN LiquidityRow WITH investor IS "absent", purchaseAmount IS 0, method IS "absent", liquidityPrice IS 0, conversionShares IS 0, perShare IS 0, entitlement IS 0, paid IS 0

#EVAL liquidity `before any round` `acquired for 10m`
#ASSERT `close to` ((liquidity `before any round` `acquired for 10m`)'s liquidityCapitalization) 11_235_293 0.0001
#ASSERT (`liquidity row for` (liquidity `before any round` `acquired for 10m`) "Investor A")'s method EQUALS "convert"
#ASSERT (`liquidity row for` (liquidity `before any round` `acquired for 10m`) "Investor B")'s method EQUALS "convert"
#ASSERT (`liquidity row for` (liquidity `before any round` `acquired for 10m`) "Investor A")'s conversionShares EQUALS 561_764
#ASSERT (`liquidity row for` (liquidity `before any round` `acquired for 10m`) "Investor B")'s conversionShares EQUALS 1_123_529
#ASSERT `close to` ((liquidity `before any round` `acquired for 10m`)'s perShareConsideration) 0.8901 0.0005
#ASSERT `close to` ((`liquidity row for` (liquidity `before any round` `acquired for 10m`) "Investor A")'s paid) 500_026 0.0005
#ASSERT `close to` ((`liquidity row for` (liquidity `before any round` `acquired for 10m`) "Investor B")'s paid) 1_000_053 0.0005

§§ `Q4 — acquired for $3m cash`

-- "The per share cash consideration, if the safes convert, is $0.2670 … neither safe would
--  convert since the safe holders’ pro rata share of the cash consideration is less than
--  their Purchase Amount … After the safe holders are paid back, the remaining cash
--  consideration of $2m is shared pro rata among all other stockholders." — p. 22

`acquired for 3m` MEANS LiquidityIn WITH
    proceeds                         IS 3_000_000
    indebtedness                     IS 0
    promisedOptionsReceivingProceeds IS 0

#EVAL liquidity `before any round` `acquired for 3m`
#ASSERT (`liquidity row for` (liquidity `before any round` `acquired for 3m`) "Investor A")'s method EQUALS "cash-out"
#ASSERT (`liquidity row for` (liquidity `before any round` `acquired for 3m`) "Investor B")'s method EQUALS "cash-out"
#ASSERT (`liquidity row for` (liquidity `before any round` `acquired for 3m`) "Investor A")'s paid EQUALS 200_000
#ASSERT (`liquidity row for` (liquidity `before any round` `acquired for 3m`) "Investor B")'s paid EQUALS 800_000
-- what the guide calls the per-share consideration "if the safes convert": 3m over the
-- all-converting Liquidity Capitalization; asserted through the row's liquidityPrice basis
-- is not possible once nobody converts, so assert the remaining cash instead.
#ASSERT `close to` ((liquidity `before any round` `acquired for 3m`)'s perShareConsideration TIMES 9_550_000) 2_000_000 0.0001

§§ `Pending`

-- Example 2 mixes a pre-money Safe with a post-money one; its pre-money half waits for
-- the yc-safe-premoney leaf (SPEC.md §7).

§ `Synthetic cases — not from the User Guide`

-- The guide has no example with discount or MFN Safes converting beside cap Safes, and
-- none of a deal the generator must refuse. These are ours; the expected values are
-- derived by hand from the form's formulas, not from any published figure.

§§ `A mixed portfolio: cap, discount and MFN in one Series A`

`safe D` MEANS SafeIn WITH
    investor          IS `party named` "Investor D"
    purchaseAmount    IS 100_000
    date              IS "2018-10-01"
    terms             IS TermsIn WITH cap IS NOTHING, discount IS JUST 20, mfn IS NOTHING
    proRataSideLetter IS FALSE

`safe M` MEANS SafeIn WITH
    investor          IS `party named` "Investor M"
    purchaseAmount    IS 50_000
    date              IS "2018-10-01"
    terms             IS TermsIn WITH cap IS NOTHING, discount IS NOTHING, mfn IS JUST TRUE
    proRataSideLetter IS FALSE

`mixed deal` MEANS Deal WITH
    form    IS `US cap form`
    company IS `ABC`
    safes   IS LIST `safe A`, `safe B`, `safe D`, `safe M`
    round   IS JUST `series A`

#EVAL convert `mixed deal`
#ASSERT `method for` (convert `mixed deal`) "Investor D" EQUALS "discount"
#ASSERT `method for` (convert `mixed deal`) "Investor M" EQUALS "price"
-- The discount Safe converts at 80% of the round price and the MFN Safe at the round price,
-- so D gets exactly 1.25× the shares per dollar that M does.
#ASSERT `close to` (`shares for` (convert `mixed deal`) "Investor D")
                   (`shares for` (convert `mixed deal`) "Investor M" TIMES 2 TIMES 1.25) 0.0001
-- Company Capitalization still satisfies its own definition: base plus every Safe's shares.
#ASSERT `close to` ((convert `mixed deal`)'s companyCapitalization)
                   (10_000_000 PLUS sum (map (GIVEN r YIELD r's shares) ((convert `mixed deal`)'s rows))) 0.00001

-- Without a round, discount and MFN Safes have no price to convert at.
`mixed deal, no round` MEANS Deal WITH
    form    IS `US cap form`
    company IS `ABC`
    safes   IS LIST `safe A`, `safe D`, `safe M`
    round   IS NOTHING
#ASSERT `method for` (convert `mixed deal, no round`) "Investor D" EQUALS "none"
#ASSERT `method for` (convert `mixed deal, no round`) "Investor A" EQUALS "cap"

§§ `Deals the generator must refuse`

-- A discount Safe on the valuation-cap form: the form has no Discount Rate blank.
#ASSERT NOT null (`validate deal` (Deal WITH form IS `US cap form`, company IS `ABC`, safes IS (LIST `safe D`), round IS NOTHING))

-- Singapore publishes only the valuation-cap form (SPEC.md §3.4).
`SG discount form` MEANS FormIn WITH
    family IS "postmoney", edition IS "1.2", jurisdiction IS "sg", variant IS "discount"
#ASSERT NOT null (`validate deal` (Deal WITH form IS `SG discount form`, company IS `ABC`, safes IS (LIST `safe D`), round IS NOTHING))

-- The Singapore form fixes its governing law and has a registration-number blank;
-- supplying a governing law, or omitting the number, is refused.
`SG cap form` MEANS FormIn WITH
    family IS "postmoney", edition IS "1.2", jurisdiction IS "sg", variant IS "cap"
`ABC Pte Ltd` MEANS CompanyIn WITH
    name               IS "ABC Pte. Ltd."
    incorporation      IS NOTHING
    governingLaw       IS NOTHING
    registrationNumber IS JUST "202600001K"
    address            IS ""
    email              IS ""
    signatory          IS nobody
    capTable           IS `ABC cap table`
#ASSERT null (`validate deal` (Deal WITH form IS `SG cap form`, company IS `ABC Pte Ltd`, safes IS (LIST `safe A`), round IS NOTHING))
#ASSERT NOT null (`validate deal` (Deal WITH form IS `SG cap form`, company IS `ABC`, safes IS (LIST `safe A`), round IS NOTHING))

-- A cap at or below the Purchase Amount is refused.
#ASSERT NOT null (`validate deal` (Deal WITH form IS `US cap form`, company IS `ABC`, safes IS (LIST (SafeIn WITH investor IS `party named` "X", purchaseAmount IS 5_000_000, date IS "2026-01-01", terms IS `cap terms` 4_000_000, proRataSideLetter IS FALSE)), round IS NOTHING))

§ `MFN Amendment Provision — three traces`

-- "promptly" taken as 5 days. Day 0: the Company issues more favorable securities.

-- Notice on day 2, election on day 9 (within 10 of the notice), restatement on day 12.
#TRACE `MFN Amendment Provision` 5 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `provide the MFN Notice` AT 2
    PARTY Investor DOES `notify the Company that the terms are preferable` AT 9
    PARTY Company DOES `amend and restate this Safe to be identical` AT 12

-- Election on day 14 is outside the 10-day window: the permission lapses, nothing is owed.
#TRACE `MFN Amendment Provision` 5 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `provide the MFN Notice` AT 2
    PARTY Investor DOES `notify the Company that the terms are preferable` AT 14

-- Election in time, but the Company never restates: breach by the Company.
#TRACE `MFN Amendment Provision` 5 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `provide the MFN Notice` AT 2
    PARTY Investor DOES `notify the Company that the terms are preferable` AT 9
